  nonce: 72da  # 72da
  message: "BEARING FROM WI-sofuh (branch jgstern-agent/fix/sofuh, commit 4b50aaba1a, NOT integrated). Checked whether the bare-identifier fix touches this path: it does NOT change the member-call Case 2 site this item names (js_ts.py `elif obj_name and obj_name in namespace_imports:`), nor the `new ns.C()` sites. Those still qualify `cp.exec(cmd)` with the import whenever the receiver ROOT name matches.\n\nWhat the branch DOES change, and is the bare-call half of this mechanism: a bare call is now resolved by a scope walk (`_ScopeBinder`, position-based). A local VALUE shadowing a destructured import -- `const { exec } = require('child_process'); function f() { const exec = make(); exec(c); }` -- used to emit javascript:child_process:0-0:exec:unresolved through the named-import arm; it now emits nothing (pinned: test_js_ts_bare_name_scope_binding.py::TestLocalBindingsAreNotResolvedByName, five shadow spellings: param, local, destructured param, for-of, catch). Parameters were already guarded by the old `_is_shadowed_by_param`, which the binder replaces.\n\nTHE FIX FOR THIS ITEM IS NOW SMALL ON THAT BRANCH: in Case 2, consult `binder.bind(obj_node, obj_name)` first and skip the namespace qualification when it returns `local` (a parameter or local value); an `import` binding (incl. a lazy `require` inside the function, which IS the module) keeps it. The same call guards the two `new ns.X()` sites. Not done there: out of that branch's measured scope."  # 72da
